*======================================================================
* wsymdef.a99 - the meaning stage's constants (M5 part 4): the tables'
* SAMS pages, the kinds of symbol, the variables and the error codes.
* The tables themselves are described in wsym.a99.
*======================================================================
HBPG   EQU  32
SYMPG  EQU  33                 8 pages: 1023 symbols
SYMMAX EQU  1024
NAMPG  EQU  41                 2 pages of names
NAMEND EQU  43
OBJPG  EQU  43                 8 pages: 1000 objects (MAX_OBJECTS)
HPPG   EQU  51                 4 pages: 4095 cells
HPMAX  EQU  4096
DHPG   EQU  55
DICPG  EQU  56                 4 pages: 1023 words
DICMAX EQU  1024
WRNPG  EQU  60                 682 warnings
WRNMAX EQU  680
VRBPG  EQU  61                 512 verbs
VRBMAX EQU  512
KEYMX  EQU  64
* kinds of symbol (dump.symbols writes them by name)
K.CON  EQU  1
K.GLO  EQU  2
K.ARR  EQU  3
K.ATT  EQU  4
K.PRO  EQU  5
K.CLA  EQU  6
K.OBJ  EQU  7
K.ROU  EQU  8
K.PIC  EQU  9
K.MUS  EQU  10
K.SND  EQU  11
* the meaning stage's variables (the parser's, free by now)
SV0    EQU  VOICES
SSTK   EQU  SV0+0              the return stack at the overlay's entry
SN     EQU  SV0+2              symbols
NHPG   EQU  SV0+4              the name heap's next byte: page ...
NHOF   EQU  SV0+6              ... and offset
HPN    EQU  SV0+8              the heap's next cell
ON     EQU  SV0+10             objects
VN     EQU  SV0+12             verbs
DN     EQU  SV0+14             dictionary words
WN     EQU  SV0+16             warnings
KEYL   EQU  SV0+18             the name in KEYB / NAMB: its length
EFPG   EQU  SV0+20             the page window E shows (0: not known)
SRET1  EQU  SV0+22
SRET2  EQU  SV0+24
SRET3  EQU  SV0+26
SRET4  EQU  SV0+28
STK1   EQU  SV0+30
STK2   EQU  SV0+32
STK3   EQU  SV0+34
ELINE  EQU  SV0+36             where an error or warning would be: line ...
EFILE  EQU  SV0+38             ... and file
DWL    EQU  SV0+40             DWORD: the word's length (all of it)
DWSP   EQU  SV0+42             DWORD: nonzero if it has a space
ESV1   EQU  SV0+44             EMAP: registers kept
ESV2   EQU  SV0+46
ESV3   EQU  SV0+48
ERET   EQU  SV0+50
HERE   EQU  SV0+52             the first declaration kept (sema.py's "here")
OPL    EQU  SV0+54             OPRD: the length
OLDR10 EQU  SV0+56             R10 before the overlay's own stack
ACN    EQU  SV0+58             actions (overlay 4 makes them; later stages use them)
GRN    EQU  SV0+60             GRAMTAB's length
MSTKT  EQU  >3800              the meaning stage's return stack: 2K down from
*                              here, over the lexer's and parser's buffers
*                              (free by now): its checks recurse deeply
OPB    EQU  ULIT+96            8 bytes: OPRD's string (an operator, a Const's word)
* (the overlays' own variables start at SV0+66)
KEYB   EQU  IBUF               64 bytes: a name in capitals
NAMB   EQU  IBUF+64            64 bytes: the name as written
DWB    EQU  IBUF+128           16 bytes: a dictionary word, lower case

* ---- the meaning stage's errors (WBERR, stage 4) and warnings ----------------
* (each matches one of sema.py's messages; tests/m5_sema_test.py maps them)
SE.BLT EQU  41                 is a built-in function and cannot be declared
SE.DUP EQU  42                 is already declared
SE.GLO EQU  43                 more than 240 globals
SE.ATT EQU  44                 more than 48 attributes
SE.PRO EQU  45                 more than 63 properties
SE.OBJ EQU  46                 more than 1000 objects
SE.SLF EQU  47                 the constant ... is defined in terms of itself
SE.CWO EQU  48                 the value of ... must be worked out when compiling
SE.DIV EQU  49                 division by zero
SE.NCL EQU  50                 ... is not a class
SE.CYC EQU  51                 the class ... includes itself
SE.NOB EQU  52                 ... is not an object, so nothing can be IN it
SE.TWO EQU  53                 ... is given two parents
SE.UAT EQU  54                 unknown attribute
SE.CIN EQU  55                 a class cannot say what its objects are IN
SE.UPR EQU  56                 unknown property ... (declare it with PROPERTY)
SE.UNK EQU  57                 unknown name
SE.SLV EQU  58                 SELF has no value outside a routine
SE.PVL EQU  59                 a property value must be a number, a string ...
SE.DWD EQU  60                 a dictionary word cannot be empty or contain spaces
SE.LOP EQU  61                 ... is inside itself (through IN)
SE.RPL EQU  62                 REPLACE ..., but this file has no ROUTINE ...
SE.EXT EQU  63                 EXTEND "...": no VERB has that word
SW.LNG EQU  1                  warning: longer than 12 letters
SW.SLF EQU  2                  warning: SELF in a routine that is not a property
SW.NNM EQU  3                  warning: ... has no NAME words


* the meaning stage's second half (wsema2.a99)
DVBPG  EQU  63                 each dictionary word's VERB
DSPG   EQU  116                the dictionary sorted
DNPG   EQU  117                each word's place
VTBPG  EQU  118                VERBTAB
DVTPG  EQU  119                DICTVERB
ACTPG  EQU  120                4 pages: 224 actions
ACMAX  EQU  224
LOCPG  EQU  124                a routine's locals
LOCMAX EQU  56
GRMPG  EQU  125                3 pages: GRAMTAB
GRMMAX EQU  3072
* BPROPL (PROPLEN's place in BUILTN; PROPWORD follows) is in gen/opcodes.a99,
* generated from sema.py's BUILTINS
SE.ASB EQU  64                 the action ... has no routine ...Sub
SE.VWD EQU  65                 "..." is already a word of another VERB
SE.GTK EQU  66                 ... is not a grammar token (noun, held, multi ...) or an attribute
SE.FLT EQU  67                 ... is not a routine (a grammar token's filter)
SE.TWS EQU  68                 a grammar line takes at most two objects
SE.LTW EQU  69                 ... is declared twice in this routine
SE.LCS EQU  70                 more than 16 parameters and locals in one routine
SE.LPV EQU  71                 the loop variable ... must be a LOCAL
SE.NOP EQU  72                 ... on its own does nothing
SE.NVR EQU  73                 ... is a ..., not a variable: it cannot be assigned to
SE.ARE EQU  74                 only an array element can be assigned to with ( )
SE.IDX EQU  75                 an array element takes one index
SE.NVL EQU  76                 ... is a ... and has no value here
SE.HAS EQU  77                 HAS / HASNT needs an attribute name after it
SE.UPX EQU  78                 unknown property ... (after a dot)
SE.ARG EQU  79                 ... takes n arguments, not m
SE.PAR EQU  80                 the second argument of ... must be a property name
SE.NCA EQU  82                 ... is a ... and cannot be called

* the code generator (wcode.a99, overlay 5): pages no window maps by
* default (0, 1, 4-9) and the REPLACE page, free by then
FIXPG  EQU  6                  2 pages: 1024 fixups
FIXMAX EQU  1024
STRPG  EQU  8                  448 strings
STRMAX EQU  448
RDIRPG EQU  9                  512 routines
RDMAX  EQU  512
LABPG  EQU  62                 a routine's labels (511) and jumps (768)
LABMAX EQU  511
JMPMAX EQU  768
CODMAX EQU  16384              the code: pages 0, 1, 4, 5 (CODAT)
SE.MAIN EQU 83                 there is no ROUTINE Main: the game starts there
SE.ACT EQU  84                 rule cases need the library's global "action"
SE.CNC EQU  85                 cannot compile Case (a case outside a rule block)

* the linker (wlink.a99, wlink2.a99: overlays 6 and 7)
IMGEND EQU  112                the image ends before the declaration index
LFXPG  EQU  124                the tables' fixups: 8 bytes (place hi, lo, kind, key)
LFXMAX EQU  512
WHRPG  EQU  62                 where things went (packed addresses): routines by
*                              place in RDIRPG (+0), strings (+1024), routines
*                              by symbol (+2048)
ABBPG  EQU  60                 the 128 substitutions: 8 bytes each (+0 length,
*                              +2 the text's place here, +4 the next in its
*                              chain + 1, +6 hash), 64 chains at +1024, the
*                              texts from +1152
FLGOFF EQU  2048               DVBPG +2048: each dictionary word's flags byte
* (variables: what both overlays keep, in ULIT; their own from SV0+66)
IMGPG  EQU  ULIT+0             the image's first page
IPH    EQU  ULIT+2             the next byte's place, high word ...
IPL    EQU  ULIT+4             ... and low
IPCUR  EQU  ULIT+58            the image page IPAGE last showed (IBYTE's fast path)
LFN    EQU  ULIT+6             the tables' fixups
NABB   EQU  ULIT+8             substitutions chosen
ISVH   EQU  ULIT+10
ISVL   EQU  ULIT+12
IRET   EQU  ULIT+14
IRET2  EQU  ULIT+16
IRET3  EQU  ULIT+18
IRET4  EQU  ULIT+20
IRET5  EQU  ULIT+22
ITMP   EQU  ULIT+24
ITMP2  EQU  ULIT+26
ABBTXT EQU  ULIT+28            ABBPG: the next free byte for texts
* the code generator's results, kept for the linker (GLOBRM: no overlay clears it)
CTOP   EQU  GLOBRM+>40         the code's length
RN     EQU  GLOBRM+>42         routines
FXN    EQU  GLOBRM+>44         fixups
STRN   EQU  GLOBRM+>46         strings
WDATE  EQU  GLOBRM+>38         6 bytes: the build date, yymmdd, as given at
*                              the prompt (the TI has no clock; zeros until then)
WDLEN  EQU  GLOBRM+>48         the date being typed: its length ...
WDBUF  EQU  GLOBRM+>4A         ... and its 6 digits
WDRET  EQU  GLOBRM+>50         WDOK's return
SE.ROOM EQU 86                 not enough SAMS for the story image (the workbench's limit)
SE.P255 EQU 87                 a property holds at most 255 words
SE.DYN EQU  88                 the dynamic area is ... bytes; the limit is 16384
SE.TAB EQU  89                 the tables before the routines pass 64K
SE.IMG EQU  90                 the story is ... bytes; the limit is ...
SE.DSK EQU  91                 a disk error writing the story (the DSR's code in WBERRL)

* the progress line (wsym.a99: PSTAGE, PSTEP)
PROW   EQU  5                  its row
PCOL   EQU  37                 the bar's column: 40 cells, dots filling with #
PCELLS EQU  40
PDONE  EQU  GLOBRM+>52         cells drawn
PSAV   EQU  GLOBRM+>54         18 bytes: registers kept (to GLOBRM+>65)
PTOT   EQU  GLOBRM+>66         the parser's token stream: its length
WPFX   EQU  GLOBRM+>6C         the project's game prefix: a length byte, 6 letters
*                              (to GLOBRM+>72; M6 part 3: the story's and the
*                              engine's file names)
EFN1   EQU  >3700              an error's fields, in VRAM (M6 part 6): a name or word
EFN2   EQU  >3728              ... a second (a length byte, then the text)
EFA    EQU  >3740              ... numbers
EFB    EQU  >3742
EFF    EQU  >3744              ... another declaration's file (index) and line
EFL    EQU  >3746
EFEND  EQU  >3748
EFTMP  EQU  GLOBRM+>1C0        (EFNUM's word)
EFRET  EQU  GLOBRM+>1C2        (EFNAMB's return)
EFSAV  EQU  GLOBRM+>1C4        (EFNAMB: R1-R3, 6 bytes)
WBBLD  EQU  GLOBRM+>74         after the compile: 1 Build (the engine's files), 2 test-play, 3 Build then Run (R)
WBRDY  EQU  GLOBRM+>3E         the game built since the last compile: 0 no, 1 yes, 2 being built for R (runs at the end)
TINAME EQU  GLOBRM+>170        22 bytes: a TI Artist picture's name, a length
*                              byte first ("DSK1.BIRD": its files are DSK1.BIRD_P,
*                              _C and _T; overlays 8 and 12); 0: none.  (GLOBRM
*                              holds a story's globals only in the engine)
LKTEND EQU  GLOBRM+>186        the statistics (S): the tables' end (where the
*                              routines start), 0 until a compile links
LKIPG  EQU  GLOBRM+>188        ... and the image's first page
OPCOL  EQU  GLOBRM+>18A        the options (O, overlay 14; DSK1.TXAOPT): the colour
*                              scheme, 0-4 (0 gray on black, as at first)
OPFNT  EQU  GLOBRM+>18C        ... the font: 0 normal, 1 bold
OPLSTR EQU  GLOBRM+>18E        ... 22 bytes: the library devices, a length byte, then
*                              up to 20 characters ("DSK2. DSK3."): where an INCLUDE's
*                              file is looked for when its own device lacks it
